## The ticket, re-read at source and re-measured at main `e027ebd0` (MEASURED-BY-DRAFTER; re-measure every line)
Jira read 2026-10-23 (MPSCALC-229, Backlog, label `needs-ruling`, now ruled). Code read from the main tarball.
- **MPSCALC-229 (reproduces).** `Proposal.cs:~520-545` (`CopyPurchase`, the block under the comment "MPSCALC-214 ... the deal's applied mono and colour click replace the section rates"): for a deal-usage quote (`p.Usage is { } u`) it builds `counted` = the section ids holding a non-optional, non-credit device line (X-25), then for each device class of those sections emits one mono row and, whenever `u.AppliedColourClick is decimal colour`, one colour row, so a class whose counted lines estimate no colour pages (the ticket's case (a): a large-format class with mono pages only) still prints "a colour rate per page". `PurchaseLineResultDto` carries `MonoPagesPerDeviceMonth`/`ColourPagesPerDeviceMonth`, `Quantity`, `ItemClass`, `Optional`, `Credit`, `SectionId` (`Dtos.cs:976ff`), and the section carries `DeviceClass`. The existing rows `B103DealUsageProposalTests.cs` (the `UsageRates` rows at `:129-135` and neighbours) pin today's per-class pairs. The engine charges the deal's colour click on every counted line's colour pages (X-25, `ENGINE.md:141`), so a class with 0 colour pages is charged nothing for colour, and the customer is told a colour rate against it.
- **What "estimated colour pages" means (read the engine before you decide; record it):** a class has estimated colour pages when the sum over its counted lines of `Quantity` x `ColourPagesPerDeviceMonth` is greater than 0 (the engine's own deal-usage page arithmetic is `PurchaseCalculator.cs:701ff`; use ITS definition, do not invent one). A line with `ColourPagesPerDeviceMonth` null counts as 0.
- **A guard you must respect:** `Proposal.cs` documents "Every field read is a Proposal field of `ProposalAllowList.Sources`" and `Proposal.Binding.Fields["ProposalDto.UsageRates"]` lists `PurchaseResultDto.Clicks` and `PurchaseResultDto.Usage` (`B103DealUsageProposalTests.cs:153`). Reading the lines' colour pages to DECIDE whether a row prints reads fields the allow-list classifies; do the classification in the allow-list the way the file does it (add the binding, extend the allow-list guard rows), and do not print a page count, a volume or any figure derived from them. A guard test turning red because of your read is expected and is edited only in the binding rows it names (list them).


